{
  "_comment": [
    "Pinned model registry for Speak-AI. ModelManager will refuse to install",
    "any entry whose sha256 is not a valid 64-char hex digest, so a new model",
    "cannot ship without someone deliberately pinning it.",
    "",
    "To populate or update a hash, run:  python scripts/populate_manifest.py",
    "That downloads each artefact, records its real digest, and rewrites this",
    "file. Hashes are intentionally NOT hand-written — a hash nobody verified",
    "is worse than no hash at all, because it looks trustworthy.",
    "",
    "Updating a model is a reviewed pull request that changes url + sha256 +",
    "upstream_version together. There is deliberately no auto-update path: a",
    "surprise 145 MB download during a lesson is not acceptable on a school",
    "connection."
  ],
